From fa6aea58d55944222154b53b90677e5f1e9a72d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:52:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] COMPK-SETUPA (web): every component of 12 setup pages checked
 (5,730 components, each with a verdict) -- Configuration saves again (golden
 Exit -> FormClose question), ContactForce wired, golden keypad limits,
 Contact's post-entry clamp, disabled edits open no keypad, saves golden does
 not ask about no longer ask

* Config.Configuration: golden's only save path on this machine is Exit -> FormClose "Config data save to define?" -> YES
  (golden's own question, cConfiguration FormClose); the web Exit only closed the window, so changes were lost. New
  ht9045_config_exit_c.js: YES = editlist.save IniConfig then close, NO = close without saving. N04 host name / IPs shown.
* Setup.ContactForce: was a picture only -- GOLDEN_BRIDGE 'ContactForce' + new ht9045_contactforce_c.js (panels from
  extra.panels, trackbar -> LoadRate, Button1 calculation, btSave -> editlist.save).
* New ht9045_golden_kb_unwired.js: golden keypad flags / ranges for ~50 cells (Config edA32_1 / edHeadCondition1-3 / edA22_3 /
  edD25_* / edD60_56mm, Contact, TesterIF dependent maxima, TrayForm 27 cells, DIO pulse widths); Contact's runtime-formula
  limits and golden edDropWaitTimeMouseDown clamp from C++ extra.kb / extra.clamp; edDoubleForce -> CountDieForceKg(false).
* ht9045_wire_engine.js: GB_NO_ASK + TestIF_File_QAMode, Ld_UldDelayTime, UserDefForm_File, DeviceForm_File, TTLCfg,
  TestIF_File_TesterIF, ContactForce, TestIF_File_AGV (golden saves without YES/NO); AI(W906-KB-DISABLED) a disabled edit
  (or inside an aria-disabled container) opens no keypad (VCL: no OnMouseDown).
* Setup.Configuration / Setup.DIOInterFaceCFG are orphan pages (nothing opens them) -> redirect to the Config.* page.
* Not ported, greyed with the reason: Contact's contact / auto-height / step test set, Config btnA71Manually /
  btnUploadAll / btnN35_Test, Config.DIO spbLoad. Not wired (EastSun to decide): golden's ADAM_WriteVoltage EP writes.
C++ side: machine 2a06d6e (FileRW/IniConfig_N04.cpp, FileRW/DeviceForm_KbExtra.cpp, ctest SetupA_KbExtraN04).

Verified: syntax OK (15 scripts); helper's headless Edge 49/49; o2 wb_serve 0 errors; ctest SetupA_KbExtraN04 (32),
B8_CtL2_TimerEP, HSys_HeaterMix, WebLogin_Reauth, EBoot005_CustomerName, CompK_DataS, S98_CfgTrayPlate 7/7; audit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
